course: dictionary
lesson: 5227
title: Jerk: a sudden, rough movement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jerk can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to jerk means to move or pull suddenly and roughly. As a noun, a jerk is a quick, sudden movement or pull. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «The bus jerked forward» is a verb, and «with a jerk» is a noun.
explain: «A knee-jerk reaction» is a quick answer or action made without thinking. Context helps here: knee-jerk is a reflex, a quick automatic movement that does not wait for the brain. Your leg kicks before you have thought about it.
explain: Be careful with the rude meaning. Jerk can also mean a mean or stupid person. It is an insult, so it is not polite to call someone a jerk. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each one in the sentence and see which makes sense.
fact: Jerk can be a verb (to jerk) or a noun (a jerk).
fact: «Jerk» means to move or pull suddenly and roughly.
fact: «A jerk» can mean a quick, sudden movement or pull.
fact: A reflex, like the knee-jerk, is a quick movement that happens without waiting for your brain.
fact: Jerk in the rude sense means a mean or stupid person, and it is not polite to use it about people.
exercise: «The bus jerked forward at the traffic lights.» What does jerked mean? | Stopped slowly and gently | *Moved suddenly and roughly | Sang loudly | Floated softly
exercise: «A knee-jerk reaction» is a quick answer given without thinking. What does knee-jerk suggest? | A sore knee from running | A dance move | A slow answer after careful thought | *A quick answer given without thinking
exercise: «A tsunami is a series of huge waves made when the sea floor jerking up or down in an undersea earthquake.» Find and copy one word that means moves suddenly. | series | undersea | waves | *jerking
test: «Ben felt a jerk on the rope as the boat pulled away.» What is a jerk here? | *A sudden pull | A loud song | A long, slow walk | A kind friend
test: Ruby said, «Don't call people a jerk, it's rude.» What does jerk mean in that sentence? | A happy dance | *A mean or stupid person | A tall tree | A quick movement
exam: «The Crocodile would jerk him into the river before you can say Jack Robinson.» What does jerk mean here? | *To pull suddenly and roughly | To sing softly | To sleep for a long time | To paint a picture
